  "id": "error-analysis",
  "term": "error analysis",
  "definition": "Error analysis is the examination of how predicted speech sounds differ from target sounds so that patterns of mistakes can be identified and summarized. In this context, it is used at the phoneme level to describe confusion patterns, transition-related features, and other interpretable measures of speech performance.",
